+# Shared bundle writer batch
+
+Base: `aa3a685f4725f7b12c2d96be252a77c94097ad12` (the completed build-boundary batch).
+This source delivery includes that batch and all earlier upstream changes.
+
+## Changes
+
+- Captured 15 golden writer outputs before extraction: RPM, APT and Arch,
+  each with fresh, reused, corrupt-cache, differential and additive payloads.
+  They compare payload-directory contents, complete record text, JSON key order,
+  checksums, provenance, assurance and ordered log/item/progress events. Only
+  fixture clocks, source IDs, temporary roots and platform line endings are
+  normalized. Synthetic payloads establish writer parity, not native installation.
+- Fixed Arch cache handling: reporting callback failures during verifying,
+  reused or progress notifications propagate instead of invalidating a cached
+  package. Corrupt Arch payloads now log an explicit recovery message. Three
+  regression cases failed before the fix and passed afterward. The only changed
+  golden expectation is the new Arch corrupt-cache log message.
+- Delegated APT transfers to the existing common transfer implementation, retaining
+  its `_copy_or_download` entry point and module-local URL opener and verifier
+  hooks. Defaults resolve at call time; shared globals are not temporarily changed.
+  Original transport URLs still reach the opener; existing credential redaction
+  continues to apply to displayed URLs. Repository provenance remains visible.
+- Delegated APT provenance emission to the existing common writer, preserving its
+  wrapper, signing, additive merging, differential warning and assurance legend.
+  Replaced the duplicated authority-unknown literal with the existing constant.
+- Added immutable package-family conventions and shared acquisition/record writers.
+  All three backends now use the same cache/transfer loop and common record-file
+  emission. Family event ordering, reuse logging, filenames, record newlines and
+  optional-file retention remain compatible. Pacman signature sidecars remain in
+  SHA256SUMS while package summaries continue to exclude them.
+- Kept manifest rows and summaries, provenance assertions, repository emitters,
+  installation contracts and installers in their original backends. RPM's leading
+  `nevra` field, APT archive-chain semantics and Arch signature fields are preserved.
+- Preserved package types through baseline partitioning and acquisition callbacks.
+  Both new modules have strict annotations and are tested with Tk imports blocked.
+- Added regression coverage for cancellation, transfer failures, cleanup, APT hook
+  compatibility, record edges and callback failures across all three families.
+  Replaced a source-text assurance test with an actual writer/output check.
+
+## Validation and evidence
+
+`validation/bundle-refactor-gate/SUMMARY.md` is the final release result; its JSON
+records every test and source revision. Static and focused results, the before-fix
+regression output, patches and archive checks are in `validation/bundle-refactor/`.
+
+Intermediate attempts are retained for audit. The first delegation gate stopped
+when the local virtual display failed to initialize. After correcting that setup,
+its rerun caught a source-text test requiring APT's former duplicated helper call.
+That test now executes both public provenance writers and checks their actual
+assurance output. Focused golden and failure checks cover the extraction; only the
+final full-tree gate establishes the completed batch's release result. No failed
+intermediate run is counted as passing evidence.
+
+## Scope and remaining work
+
+This completes the common writer portion of instruction item 7. It does not merge
+resolvers, version comparators or inventory parsers. A dispatch-registry rewrite
+(item 7.5) remains separate: the existing typed dispatch preserves repository-format
+precedence, and removing a few branches here would add risk without improving the
+writer boundary. No GUI layout or release/version selection behavior is changed.
+
+The upstream Windows Python/Tk bootstrap failure recorded in BUILD-BOUNDARY.md is
+outside this batch. Local Linux tests and a source ZIP smoke check do not certify
+Windows native execution or a frozen/signed Windows release. This work is committed
+locally; it has not been pushed to GitHub.
